1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,140
Hi and welcome back to Act Last time we
looked

2
00:00:04,140 --> 00:00:07,660
at the roles you have and the communities
those roles connect you to

3
00:00:08,340 --> 00:00:12,460
Now imagine looking at one of those
communities more closely You

4
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:16,220
will probably notice two things at the
same time things that are working

5
00:00:16,220 --> 00:00:20,340
well and things that could be better
Social awareness

6
00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:24,080
means learning to notice both If you only
see problems

7
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:28,280
you miss the strengths already available
If you only see strengths

8
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:32,760
you may ignore people who are struggling
Understanding a community

9
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:36,400
means holding both views together Both
matter

10
00:00:37,120 --> 00:00:40,540
One way people contribute to a community
is through volunteering

11
00:00:41,340 --> 00:00:45,680
Volunteering is work a person gives to
society without expecting a reward

12
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:49,820
in return That does not mean the volunteer
learns nothing or

13
00:00:49,820 --> 00:00:54,320
gains nothing personally People may
develop skills experience

14
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:58,840
or stronger connections through service
The difference is the purpose

15
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:03,660
the action begins with contributing to a
need not with demanding a

16
00:01:03,660 --> 00:01:07,780
reward Volunteering is one way a person
can turn awareness

17
00:01:07,780 --> 00:01:11,940
of a community into useful action even
when the action itself is

18
00:01:11,940 --> 00:01:16,020
small That makes contribution practical
Think about

19
00:01:16,020 --> 00:01:20,180
a simple example A fallen tree blocks a
road and

20
00:01:20,180 --> 00:01:24,300
one child starts trying to move it The
child cannot solve the problem

21
00:01:24,300 --> 00:01:27,820
alone at first but the action gets other
people moving too

22
00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:32,020
The useful point is not that one person
must do everything

23
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:36,840
It is that initiative can begin when
someone notices a problem and

24
00:01:36,840 --> 00:01:41,140
takes a reasonable first step Sometimes
other people choose to join

25
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:45,360
once they see that action is possible A
community can change

26
00:01:45,360 --> 00:01:49,740
when awareness moves from someone should
do something to what

27
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:54,060
useful step can begin here That shift is
what initiative

28
00:01:54,060 --> 00:01:58,340
looks like Contribution can benefit both
the community and

29
00:01:58,340 --> 00:02:02,340
the person contributing A community may
gain a cleaner space

30
00:02:02,740 --> 00:02:06,900
better support useful knowledge or help
with a problem At

31
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:11,240
the same time the person involved may
practice communication organization

32
00:02:11,800 --> 00:02:16,260
problem solving or another skill Imagine
people helping improve

33
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:19,840
buildings in their village while learning
practical construction skills

34
00:02:19,840 --> 00:02:24,040
through the process The point is not to
promise a job or a

35
00:02:24,040 --> 00:02:28,060
reward It is to show that serving a real
need can also

36
00:02:28,060 --> 00:02:31,660
become a place where useful abilities are
practiced and strengthened

37
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:36,060
A useful way to understand a community is
to map what you see

38
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:40,900
Use green spots for strengths and
opportunities red spots for

39
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:45,160
problems or negative conditions and black
points for possible reasons

40
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:48,840
behind a problem A green spot might be
supportive people

41
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:52,560
useful resources local knowledge or a good
facility

42
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:56,960
A red spot might be littering unemployment
smoking

43
00:02:57,440 --> 00:03:01,760
unsafe spaces or another issue affecting
people A black point

44
00:03:01,760 --> 00:03:06,740
asks a different question what may be
contributing to that problem The

45
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:10,860
map helps you separate what is good what
is difficult and what may be

46
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:14,240
behind it Try this as an individual
reflection

47
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:19,080
Choose one community you know well your
neighborhood school

48
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:23,280
university workplace or another place you
regularly see

49
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:28,000
Picture it like a simple map First mark
two or

50
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,020
three green spots strengths resources or
opportunities

51
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:36,660
Then mark two or three red spots problems

52
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:40,560
or difficulties you have genuinely noticed
For one red spot

53
00:03:40,980 --> 00:03:45,240
write one possible reason beside it You
are not trying to prove

54
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:49,340
the cause yet The goal is to separate what
you observe from what

55
00:03:49,340 --> 00:03:53,580
you think may be causing it That
distinction matters Now

56
00:03:53,580 --> 00:03:57,620
add one more layer where could your own
abilities fit

57
00:03:58,360 --> 00:04:02,020
Maybe you are good at explaining ideas
organizing information

58
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:06,300
listening designing writing technology

59
00:04:06,920 --> 00:04:11,060
sports or practical work You do not need
to solve

60
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:15,300
every red spot on the map Contribution
starts by noticing

61
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:18,960
where a real need and a useful ability
might connect

62
00:04:19,620 --> 00:04:23,780
Sometimes that connection becomes
volunteering Sometimes it becomes

63
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:27,880
an initiative later For now the important
skill is

64
00:04:27,880 --> 00:04:32,320
seeing your community as a place with both
needs and resources not

65
00:04:32,320 --> 00:04:36,500
only as a place where you happen to live
Let’s bring Unit 2

66
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:40,300
together Your roles connect you to
communities

67
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:45,320
Communities contain people resources
strengths

68
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:50,360
opportunities and problems Contribution
means noticing

69
00:04:50,360 --> 00:04:54,480
where something useful can be offered and
volunteering is one

70
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:58,540
way that can happen Keep your community
map in mind

71
00:04:58,920 --> 00:05:03,040
especially the red spots you identified In
the next part

72
00:05:03,040 --> 00:05:07,200
of Act we will choose one real problem and
slow down

73
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:11,280
before trying to solve it We will learn
how to define it clearly

74
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:15,460
and understand what is actually happening
That’s

75
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:17,760
it for today and I’ll see you in the next
lesson
